WHAT 0x7 AND 0xf ARE — from raw_object.h, not from the numbers

  UntaggedFunction          entry_point_ is the FIRST field after the header
                            -> untagged 8  -> tagged 0x7
                            unchecked_entry_point_ next
                            -> untagged 16 -> tagged 0xf
  UntaggedSingleTargetCache POINTER_FIELD(CodePtr, target) then uword entry_point_
                            -> target untagged 8, entry_point_ untagged 16
                            -> tagged 0xf

So 0x7 is unambiguous: Function::entry_point_. That is the field
--patchable_static_calls emits loads from, and the field AttachBytecode moves.

0xf is AMBIGUOUS on offset alone: Function::unchecked_entry_point_ and
SingleTargetCache::entry_point_ both land there. The offset cannot decide it.

